name the user wants to add is equal to recently removed action inside the tree. without this change, the add button will remain disabled (even though it's a valid action name), making the user feel the GUI is unresponsive.\r\n\r\n## Testing\r\n\r\n### Before Changes\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/405ac525-e392-4a13-9320-ae43eee38289\r\n\r\n### After Changes\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1e20aaeb-ff3a-4b04-905a-0e8715173159\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n- You can still add the action by clicking EditLine field, and pressing `Enter`, but I think if it's valid to do this using shortcuts, it's should be the same using UI components (through the add button in this case).\r\n- Reason behind calling the `_add_edit_text_changed` callback is because it does all the validation needed when deciding to Enable or Disable the `Add Action` button, and setting tooltip text, so calling it makes more sense then code duplication.\r\n\r\n## Use of AI\r\nNo AI was used in the process of making these changes.","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098219,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgyMTk=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:editor","name":"topic:editor","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":15520464,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4A7NLQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/25","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/25","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/25/labels","number":25,"state":"open","title":"4.8","description":"","creator":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","grava